        scheme: ["Per kg in orbit: E = −GM/2r = −3.98×10¹⁴/(2×7.0×10⁶) = −2.84×10⁷ J kg⁻¹", "At rest on the same orbit the potential is −GM/r = −5.68×10⁷ J kg⁻¹, and escape requires +5.68×10⁷ J kg⁻¹ from rest", "From orbit, the probe already holds kinetic energy +GM/2r = +2.84×10⁷ J kg⁻¹, so extra energy = 5.68×10⁷ − 2.84×10⁷ = 2.84×10⁷ J kg⁻¹", "The extra energy exactly equals the orbital kinetic energy per kg: doubling the speed escapes"],
